    q: 'What is the formula to convert UK size to EU shoes?',
    a: 'To convert UK size to EU shoes, add 34 to adult men\'s sizes (UK 8 + 34 = EU 42) or 33 to adult women\'s sizes (UK 5 + 33 = EU 38). Because British sizing uses 1/3-inch increments (8.46 mm) and European sizing uses 2/3 cm increments (6.67 mm), checking our shoe size chart uk eu provides an exact metric alignment.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do European and UK shoe sizes differ in increments?',
    a: 'Continental European sizing is built on the Paris Point (Point de Paris), which increments by 6.67 mm, while British footwear uses the imperial barleycorn standard (8.46 mm). This means European shoe sizes advance at a faster rate, allowing for finer graduations without requiring as many half sizes.'
  }
